{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"860165485579337779","content":"<@&860164792244371467> Since each of you have the option of calling the park your home, or your ship/PC house (in the case of bones) I need to point something out.  The park is considered the land of one of the wardens, and thus is effectively not part of the USA, instead part of the wilds.  Along with it being a type of holy land, its also kinda like an embassy.  It will stay just as open and free as it always has, but it has implications you have to decide on basically before epilogue for yourself, even if you don't declare it publicly, as it can influence if you decide to stay in the city, or move out went, and what rights and protections you have in those settings.\n\nSo you all have claim to be citizens of the wilds, or of USA, as per the agreement the Wardens made in the congress.\n\nIf you are married, you both have to be members of one nation or the other,you cannot split, nor have dual citizenship.\n\nSo its something for you to consider, possibly even discuss.","created_at":"2021-08-25T14:28:03.272000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"880096190753030184","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
